      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The case report describes a difficult and not uncommon situation of a patient suffering from an evolving myocardial infarction with hemodynamic instability along with a critical bilateral extracranial carotid artery stenosis. A technique of retrograde coronary sinus perfusion was used to temporarily stabilize the cardiac status while the carotid lesion was being tackled."},
